[54.912179, "o", "Occurrence: \r\n========================================\r\nOccurrence: ndividual patient can be appropriately managed\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0001||\r\n1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE\r\nPAXLOVID is indicated for the treatment of mild-to-moderate coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) in adults who a\r\n========================================\r\nOccurrence:  COVID-19, including hospitalization or death.\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0002||\r\nLimitations of Use\r\nPAXLOVID is not approved for use as pre-exposure or post-exposure prophylaxis for prevention of COVID-19 .\r\n\r\n||PASSAG\r\n========================================\r\nOccurrence: osure prophylaxis for prevention of COVID-19 .\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0003||\r\n2.1\tImportant Dosage and Administration Information\r\nPAXLOVID is nirmatrelvir tablets co-packaged with ritonavir tablets. There are thre\r\n========================================\r\nOccurrence: owed whole and not chewed, broken, or crushed.\r\n\r\n||PASSAGE_0004||\r\n2.2\tRecommended Dosage\r\nThe recommended dosage for PAXLOVID is 300 mg nirmatrelvir (two 150 mg tablets) with 100 mg ritonavir (one 100 m\r\n========================================\r\n"]
